I now have a complete picture of all the files involved. Let me compile the comprehensive analysis.

---

## 1. Architecture Overview

The change `Querier(mint, maxt int64) → Querier(ctx context.Context, mint, maxt int64)` propagates through **three repositories** (Prometheus, Thanos, Mimir) across **four architectural layers**:

```
storage.Queryable interface (Prometheus: storage/interface.go)
         │
         ├── DB.Querier (Prometheus: tsdb/db.go)          ← PRIMARY CHANGE SITE
         ├── DBReadOnly.Querier (Prometheus: tsdb/db.go)
         │
         ├── Implementations of storage.Queryable:
         │     ├── fanout.Querier (storage/fanout.go)
         │     ├── remote/Storage.Querier (storage/remote/storage.go)
         │     ├── remote/sampleAndChunkQueryableClient.Querier (storage/remote/read.go)
         │     ├── QueryableFunc adapter (storage/interface.go)
         │     ├── MockQueryable.Querier (storage/interface.go)
         │     ├── FakeQueryable.Querier (web/api/testhelpers/mocks.go)
         │     │
         │     ├── [Thanos] ReadyStorage.Querier (pkg/receive/multitsdb.go)
         │     ├── [Thanos] adapter.Querier (pkg/receive/multitsdb.go)
         │     │
         │     └── [Mimir] userTSDB.Querier (pkg/ingester/user_tsdb.go)
         │           └── LazyQueryable.Querier (pkg/storage/lazyquery/lazyquery.go)
         │
         └── Callers of .Querier(mint, maxt):
               ├── DBReadOnly.Querier → q.Querier(mint, maxt) (tsdb/db.go L682)
               ├── fanout.Querier → primary.Querier(mint, maxt) (storage/fanout.go L75,82)
               ├── remote/Storage.Querier → queryable.Querier(mint, maxt) (storage/remote/storage.go L166)
               ├── LazyQueryable.Querier → lq.q.Querier(mint, maxt) (pkg/storage/lazyquery/lazyquery.go L24)
               └── ReadyStorage.Querier → x.Querier(mint, maxt) (pkg/receive/multitsdb.go L960)
```

The `storage.Queryable` interface is the **central contract**. Every implementation and every call site must be updated simultaneously.

---

## 2. Detailed Analysis

### Layer 0 — The Interface Contract (Prometheus)

**`storage/interface.go`** (L108–L120) defines the `Queryable` interface:
```go
// CURRENT — must change:
type Queryable interface {
    Querier(mint, maxt int64) (Querier, error)
}

// NEW:
type Queryable interface {
    Querier(ctx context.Context, mint, maxt int64) (Querier, error)
}
```
Also on L262–L266, the `QueryableFunc` adapter must change:
```go
// CURRENT:
type QueryableFunc func(mint, maxt int64) (Querier, error)
func (f QueryableFunc) Querier(mint, maxt int64) (Querier, error) { return f(mint, maxt) }

// NEW:
type QueryableFunc func(ctx context.Context, mint, maxt int64) (Querier, error)
func (f QueryableFunc) Querier(ctx context.Context, mint, maxt int64) (Querier, error) { return f(ctx, mint, maxt) }
```
And `MockQueryable` on L118:
```go
// CURRENT:
func (q *MockQueryable) Querier(int64, int64) (Querier, error) { ... }
// NEW:
func (q *MockQueryable) Querier(_ context.Context, _, _ int64) (Querier, error) { ... }
```

---

### Layer 1 — Primary Implementation (Prometheus `tsdb/db.go`)

**`DB.Querier`** at L2277 — the main change site:
```go
// CURRENT:
func (db *DB) Querier(mint, maxt int64) (_ storage.Querier, err error) { ... }

// NEW:
func (db *DB) Querier(ctx context.Context, mint, maxt int64) (_ storage.Querier, err error) { ... }
```
The context can be stored or passed to `db.blockQuerierFunc` for future cancellation support.

**`DBReadOnly.Querier`** at L677 — also calls `q.Querier(mint, maxt)` on the inner `*DB`:
```go
// CURRENT:
func (db *DBReadOnly) Querier(mint, maxt int64) (storage.Querier, error) {
    q, err := db.loadDataAsQueryable(maxt)
    ...
    return q.Querier(mint, maxt)   // ← must pass ctx
}

// NEW:
func (db *DBReadOnly) Querier(ctx context.Context, mint, maxt int64) (storage.Querier, error) {
    q, err := db.loadDataAsQueryable(maxt)
    ...
    return q.Querier(ctx, mint, maxt)
}
```

---

### Layer 2 — Prometheus Internal Implementations

**`storage/fanout.go`** — `fanout.Querier` at L74 calls `Querier` on both primary and secondaries:
```go
// CURRENT:
func (f *fanout) Querier(mint, maxt int64) (Querier, error) {
    primary, err := f.primary.Querier(mint, maxt)
    ...
    querier, err := storage.Querier(mint, maxt)
}

// NEW:
func (f *fanout) Querier(ctx context.Context, mint, maxt int64) (Querier, error) {
    primary, err := f.primary.Querier(ctx, mint, maxt)
    ...
    querier, err := storage.Querier(ctx, mint, maxt)
}
```

**`storage/remote/storage.go`** — `Storage.Querier` at L159 calls `queryable.Querier(mint, maxt)` in a loop:
```go
// NEW:
func (s *Storage) Querier(ctx context.Context, mint, maxt int64) (storage.Querier, error) {
    ...
    q, err := queryable.Querier(ctx, mint, maxt)
}
```

**`storage/remote/read.go`** — `sampleAndChunkQueryableClient.Querier` at L52:
```go
// NEW:
func (c *sampleAndChunkQueryableClient) Querier(ctx context.Context, mint, maxt int64) (storage.Querier, error) { ... }
```

**`web/api/testhelpers/mocks.go`** — `FakeQueryable.Querier` at L60:
```go
// NEW:
func (f *FakeQueryable) Querier(_ context.Context, _, _ int64) (storage.Querier, error) { ... }
```

---

### Layer 3 — Thanos Implementations

**`pkg/receive/multitsdb.go`** — Two structs implement `Querier`:

`ReadyStorage.Querier` at L958:
```go
// CURRENT:
func (s *ReadyStorage) Querier(mint, maxt int64) (storage.Querier, error) {
    if x := s.get(); x != nil {
        return x.Querier(mint, maxt)
    }
    return nil, ErrNotReady
}

// NEW:
func (s *ReadyStorage) Querier(ctx context.Context, mint, maxt int64) (storage.Querier, error) {
    if x := s.get(); x != nil {
        return x.Querier(ctx, mint, maxt)
    }
    return nil, ErrNotReady
}
```

`adapter.Querier` at L999:
```go
// CURRENT:
func (a adapter) Querier(mint, maxt int64) (storage.Querier, error) {
    return a.db.Querier(mint, maxt)
}

// NEW:
func (a adapter) Querier(ctx context.Context, mint, maxt int64) (storage.Querier, error) {
    return a.db.Querier(ctx, mint, maxt)
}
```

---

### Layer 4 — Mimir Implementations

**`pkg/ingester/user_tsdb.go`** — `userTSDB.Querier` at L198:
```go
// CURRENT:
func (u *userTSDB) Querier(mint, maxt int64) (storage.Querier, error) {
    return u.db.Querier(mint, maxt)
}

// NEW:
func (u *userTSDB) Querier(ctx context.Context, mint, maxt int64) (storage.Querier, error) {
    return u.db.Querier(ctx, mint, maxt)
}
```

**`pkg/storage/lazyquery/lazyquery.go`** — `LazyQueryable.Querier` at L23:
```go
// CURRENT:
func (lq LazyQueryable) Querier(mint, maxt int64) (storage.Querier, error) {
    q, err := lq.q.Querier(mint, maxt)
    ...
}

// NEW:
func (lq LazyQueryable) Querier(ctx context.Context, mint, maxt int64) (storage.Querier, error) {
    q, err := lq.q.Querier(ctx, mint, maxt)
    ...
}
```

---

### Test Files

All test files that call `db.Querier(mint, maxt)` directly or implement `Queryable` must be updated:
- **`tsdb/db_test.go`** — The `queryHelper` function at L158 receives a `storage.Querier` already opened; the test call sites that call `db.Querier(mint, maxt)` must pass `context.Background()`.
- **`tsdb/db_append_v2_test.go`** — Same pattern.
- **`pkg/ingester/ingester_test.go`** — Tests that call `userTSDB.Querier` or `db.Querier` directly.
- **`pkg/blockbuilder/tsdb_test.go`** — Calls TSDB query APIs.
- **`pkg/receive/multitsdb_test.go`** — Tests `ReadyStorage` and `adapter`.
- **`pkg/store/tsdb_test.go`** — Tests `TSDBStore` which calls `db.ChunkQuerier` (not `Querier`, but same pattern).

